+# PR-T05 R8: Visible owned save-consent dialogs
+
+- **Baseline:** `8eca399e663156d9ff2b74be86a57f46ee13f39a`
+- **Confirmed defect:** A successfully dispatched dirty Close enters `TaskDialogIndirect`, disables the owner and creates the expected owned dialog/buttons, but the dialog and every descendant retain `visible:false` for at least 15 seconds.
+- **Source finding:** The executable embeds the required Common-Controls v6 manifest, but the process never calls `InitCommonControlsEx`. Microsoft documents that an application must call it before creating a common control. Bareline initializes COM in `WindowsPlatform::new` and later enters `TaskDialogIndirect`, but it omitted that separate Common-Controls registration prerequisite. No product code changes `WS_VISIBLE`, calls `ShowWindow`, or subclasses the owned TaskDialog; the menu theme subclass is bound only to the main HWND.
+- **Scope:** Initialize the standard common-control classes before any platform dialog can be created, propagate initialization failure through the existing platform-startup error path, and leave T05 close/discard behavior unchanged.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- Added `initialize_common_controls`, using a fully sized `INITCOMMONCONTROLSEX` with `ICC_STANDARD_CLASSES`, at the start of `WindowsPlatform::new`. Initialization occurs before the menu adapter, COM dialogs, or TaskDialog calls.
+- Added a contained idempotence regression for the Windows initialization boundary. Microsoft specifies that repeated `InitCommonControlsEx` calls are cumulative, so a second adapter/test initialization remains safe.
+- Primary API contract: <https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/commctrl/nf-commctrl-initcommoncontrolsex>.
+
+Root-owned focused command:
+
+```text
+cargo test -p bareline-platform-windows common_controls_initialization_is_idempotent --offline --locked
+```
+
+Native qualification remains required: launch one fresh process, make one exact dirty edit, invoke one Close, and prove the owned `#32770` TaskDialog plus its Save / Don't Save / Cancel controls are visible and actionable without an unrelated input. Preserve the R7 command trace to show ingress, ready state, dialog entry, and selected native ID.
